Q: scrollTop x % of total A: <p>As I checked your snippet code, you have defined :</p>
<pre><code>  theHeight = window.innerHeight;
</code></pre>
<p>Which is calculating the visible screen height. It doesn't calculate the height of html document where <code>document.height()</code> is used to calculate the actual document height. In your case you need to calcuate the real scrollable height which is:</p>
<pre><code>var maxScroll = $(document).height() - $(window).height();
var scrolling = maxScroll * 0.08;

$('html,body').animate({ scrollTop: scrolling }, 800);
</code></pre>
